      <p>The Wollensak Optical Company was established in 1899, in Rochester, NY. 
        In the early 20th century, Rochester was the center of the American optics 
        industry; home to companies like Kodak, Bausch and Lomb and other major manufacturers 
        of optical and photographic supplies. </p>
      <p>Wollensak manufactured a wide range of shutters and lenses for still photography, 
        and eventually introduced the Cine Velostigmat and Cine Raptar line of lenses 
        for use on motion picture cameras.
