      <p>After World War II, the American Bolex Company chose to supply both Wollensak 
        and Kern lenses. Wollensak lenses were of good quality construction, priced 
        much lower than Kern lenses and proved to be a popular choice with many amateurs 
        throughout the 1940s and 1950s. Listed below are some of the Cine Velostigmat 
        lenses manufactured by Wollensak for 8mm and 16mm motion picture cameras. 
      </p>
